{
  "title": "Replace the ingredient line parser's special cases with a real tokenizer/grammar",
  "description": "ramekin-core/src/ingredient_parser is ~7,100 lines of string rewriting passes (strip a marker, close a dash, borrow a food across \"or\", treat a title-case word as a brand...) that run in sequence over the raw line. \
Each pass is a special case, and each fix exposes another: PR #823 fixed \"2 -3 tsp\" dash spacing and a brand-before-\"or\" regression, and review then found, one round at a time, that \"1- 2 cans\", \"1- 2 large cans\", \"1- 15 ounce can\" and \"1- 3 ounce package\" each needed their own rule. \
The current code still reads \"large\" in \"1- 2 large cans tomatoes\" as the unit. \
Proposal: tokenize a line once (numbers, fractions, ranges, units, sizes, containers, words, punctuation) and parse amount/size/unit/item from the token stream with a small grammar, so cases like a range versus a sized package fall out of the grammar instead of needing a pass each. \
Pin today's behavior first: the ~5,400 pipeline fixtures under ramekin-core/tests/fixtures/ingredient_parsing/pipeline are the regression suite. \
Run make pipeline and review the data/ diffs; any change should be an improvement you can name. \
Coordinate with p2-calorie-architecture, which owns everything after a line is parsed (recognizing the food and its calories). \
This issue is only about turning the text into amount, unit and item.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 3,
  "type": "task",
